## Mechanism and correction

The local `autonameFixture` created a valid Set trunk and pattern codename,
but no registered Setting type; its `*autoname` tag used the default content
type. Original `Card::Rule::Cache` SQL requires a Set-typed trunk and a
Setting-typed tag. Its key construction additionally requires the pattern and
setting codenames. The selected rule lookup correctly refuses this unqualified
row. No rule reaches automatic naming, so the unchanged blank-name check fires.

Original `mod/core/set/all/autoname.rb` gates naming on `rule(:autoname).present?`,
sets the name and updates the rule's seed without ordinary rule history.
Original `lib/card/name/all.rb` advances occupied names through `name.next`.
These installed card-1.110.0 sources and their hashes were inspected directly.
The native cache source remains SHA-256
`17a240a32aed7c2ea07c69df21bfb78190a4cd501583171f2b23403de1f7736d`.

The correction adds the Setting type to this local helper and gives the
`*autoname` tag that type. It does not change `seedStandardDeck`, a shared
constructor, any production source, or any rule qualification. The existing
rule ID, content, Set trunk, codenames, seed and expected generated names stay
the same. The test text from the first `describe(` through EOF is byte-identical
to the original parent: SHA-256
`3bce6818bac57a9b247996aa8886fb04813945c2e433aea171a5accdf3c0fedc`.

All original tests run, including the named-card, blank-rule and denied-create
negative controls. Their validation outcomes, history assertions, rollback
assertions and exact expected names are unchanged. No exception is added for
unqualified rules and no malformed-rule negative is edited.

